  "history": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "text": "Fang Yuan first treats White Boar Gu and Black Boar Gu as the costly pair in the Boar Gu series while he is choosing a second Gu from the academy storage room.",
        "chapters": [
          62
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "intro",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "char_fang_yuan"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "He later pulls one from an Earth Treasury Flower Gu left in the Flower Wine Monk’s strength inheritance.",
        "chapters": [
          63
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "intro",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "gu_earth_treasury_flower_gu",
          "char_flower_wine_monk"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "In the Shang clan city stretch, while Wei Yang argues against the strength path, Fang Yuan lists black and white boar Gu among the Gu he used to modify his body and raise strength. Wei Yang then calls those Gu expensive ones that permanently increase strength.",
        "chapters": [
          280
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "strength-path-mention",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "loc_shang_clan_city",
          "char_wei_yang",
          "path_strength"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Without Gu worms that modify the body like Black Boar Gu and White Boar Gu, a Gu Master’s body is no different from a mortal’s; dao marks from such modification are what make the body extraordinary.",
        "chapters": [
          1024
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "dao-marks-from-body-modification",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "sys_gu_worms"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "In Reverse Flow River terms, using Black Boar Gu to gain a boar’s strength carves strength path dao marks into the body, so that strength still remains usable even when Gu worms cannot be activated.",
        "chapters": [
          1272
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "dao-marks-from-body-modification",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "loc_reverse_flow_river"
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
